/**
@page manual Manual

@brief Operating a running unit over its serial terminal.

This is the user-facing manual for driving a deployed Botanik unit through its ANSI
terminal: navigating the pages, using the shell, and reading the live displays. It
grows as the UI does.

@section manual_pages Navigating the pages

The terminal shows one full-screen **page** at a time, with a tab bar on the top
row. The built-in pages are:

- **Home** - the at-a-glance dashboard (site name, key readings, link and alarm
  status).
- **Status** - the detailed state view, including the live alarm list.
- **Logs** - the scrolling log, newest at the bottom.
- **Shell** - the command prompt (see below).

Switch pages with the function/navigation keys; every binding and the action it
dispatches to is listed on the @subpage md_docs_2KEYBINDINGS page.

@section manual_shell Using the shell

The **Shell** page exposes a `botanik>` prompt for inspecting and poking the running
firmware. A submitted line dispatches to the built-in command set - `help`, `stats`,
`clear`, and friends. The full list, what each does, and how a site adds its own are
on the @subpage commands page.

@section manual_boot Reading the boot

Every boot ends with a single self-test verdict on the log, so a start is never
ambiguous: `POST ok (site <name>)` on success, or a `POST failed` critical (one line
per failed check) otherwise. A failure is loud but not fatal - the unit keeps running
so the diagnostics stay readable over the terminal. The checks themselves are
documented under @ref md_docs_2POST "Built-in self-tests and asserts".

@section manual_plc_setup PLC-side setup

Some firmware settings are not compiled in - they are configured on the PLC and
published to the host over shared memory: the network interface, the NTP client, and
the MQTT client. The installer sets them in the PLC program (where retained variables
survive a reboot); the host applies them as the PLC bumps each block's serial. For the
wire layout, field meanings, and the step-by-step PLC IDE setup, see
@ref md_docs_2PLC__CONFIG "PLC configuration variables".

@section manual_todo Coming later

- **Wiring.** The typical hardware hook-up (serial console and monitor links), once the
  hardware contract settles.
*/
